==================================================================
  2. EFFECTIVE MEMORY ACCESS TIME (EMAT) WITH & WITHOUT TLB
==================================================================
Given System Parameters:
  - Main Memory Access Time (t_mem) = 100.0 ns
  - TLB Associative Lookup (t_tlb)  = 10.0 ns

A. WITHOUT TLB (Single-Level Paging):
   Every memory access requires 2 physical accesses:
   1 for Page Table entry + 1 for actual Data = 2 * 100.0 ns = 200.0 ns

B. WITH TLB (Single-Level Paging Formula):
   EMAT = h * (t_tlb + t_mem) + (1 - h) * (t_tlb + 2 * t_mem)

TLB Hit Rate    Formula Calculation       EMAT (ns)            Speedup vs No-TLB
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
80             % 0.80*(110) + 0.20*(210)         130.00 ns          1.54x
95             % 0.95*(110) + 0.05*(210)         115.00 ns          1.74x
99             % 0.99*(110) + 0.01*(210)         111.00 ns          1.80x
